# ========== CONFIGURATION ==========
# Config version: 1.2
# Config for tagarr_migrate.sh — opt-in script auto-update + path hints
#
# This file controls two closely-related things in tagarr_migrate.sh:
#   1. Which tagarr scripts should be auto-updated on every migrate run
#   2. Where those tagarr files (script + matching .conf) live on disk
#
# ============================================================================
# Mental model — one path per script, two questions per script
# ============================================================================
#
# For each tagarr script, you answer two independent questions:
#
#   Q1. "Where does this script's files live on disk?"
#       → Set AUTOUPDATE_<SCRIPT>_DIR="/path/to/dir"
#       → Or leave blank/removed = same directory as tagarr_migrate.sh
#       → People usually keep script + config together, so this directory
#         is where BOTH the .sh and its matching .conf are expected to be.
#
#   Q2. "Should I auto-update this script when migrate runs?"
#       → AUTOUPDATE_<SCRIPT>=true to enable
#       → Commented out (default) = never auto-updated; still reports its
#         own version status in its own logs when it runs.
#
# These are separate decisions. You can tell migrate where a script lives
# (so it can migrate the matching config there) without enabling auto-
# update for that script.
#
# ============================================================================
# Examples
# ============================================================================
#
#   A) Everything lives next to tagarr_migrate.sh, enable auto-update
#      for tagarr_import.sh only:
#
#        AUTOUPDATE_TAGARR_IMPORT=true
#
#   B) tagarr_import.sh + tagarr_import.conf live in /appdata/radarr/scripts,
#      and you want both the script auto-updated AND its config migrated
#      from that directory:
#
#        AUTOUPDATE_TAGARR_IMPORT=true
#        AUTOUPDATE_TAGARR_IMPORT_DIR="/appdata/radarr/scripts"
#
#   C) tagarr_recover.sh is in /opt/scripts alongside its config. You
#      want the config migrated but do NOT want the script auto-updated:
#
#        #AUTOUPDATE_TAGARR_RECOVER=true           ← stays commented
#        AUTOUPDATE_TAGARR_RECOVER_DIR="/opt/scripts"  ← DIR set alone
#
#   D) Leave a script fully untouched by migrate:
#
#        (both lines commented — default state)
#
# ============================================================================
# What happens when tagarr_migrate.sh runs
# ============================================================================
#
#   Script auto-update (per script):
#     If AUTOUPDATE_<SCRIPT>=true, the script is checked against
#     versions.json on GitHub and replaced if the remote is strictly
#     newer (sort -V gate — we never "update" to an older version).
#     Old file backed up as <script>.old in the same directory. File
#     permissions and ownership are preserved.
#
#   Config migration (per .conf file):
#     All directories mentioned in this file's AUTOUPDATE_<SCRIPT>_DIR
#     settings — plus the directory tagarr_migrate.sh itself is in —
#     are scanned for tagarr_*.conf files. Every matching config found
#     is migrated: new fields from the latest sample are added with
#     defaults, your existing values are preserved, and the old config
#     is backed up as <config>.old.
#
#     This means: if you point AUTOUPDATE_TAGARR_IMPORT_DIR at
#     /appdata/radarr/scripts, migrate will also migrate the
#     tagarr_import.conf that sits in that same directory — no need
#     to invoke migrate separately against that file.
#
#   No tagarr_migrate.conf / all settings commented:
#     No script is auto-updated. Config migration runs as normal,
#     scanning only the directory tagarr_migrate.sh is in (legacy
#     behavior). This file being absent or unconfigured is the same
#     as "opt out of all new features."
#
# ============================================================================
# Requirements and fallback
# ============================================================================
#
# Requires curl + jq. If either is missing, auto-update is skipped
# with one warning line and config migration continues normally —
# no hard failure.
#
# Rollback after an auto-update:
#   mv <script>.old <script>
# The backup lives next to the script it replaced (in that script's
# AUTOUPDATE_<SCRIPT>_DIR if set, otherwise next to tagarr_migrate.sh).

# ============================================================================
# SETTINGS — per-script enable + path
# ============================================================================

# tagarr.sh — batch Radarr release-group tagger
#AUTOUPDATE_TAGARR=true
#AUTOUPDATE_TAGARR_DIR=""

# tagarr_import.sh — Radarr Connect import-time tagger (most-used)
#AUTOUPDATE_TAGARR_IMPORT=true
#AUTOUPDATE_TAGARR_IMPORT_DIR=""

# tagarr_import_sonarr.sh — Sonarr Connect import-time tagger
#AUTOUPDATE_TAGARR_IMPORT_SONARR=true
#AUTOUPDATE_TAGARR_IMPORT_SONARR_DIR=""

# tagarr_list.sh — list movies by tag / release group
#AUTOUPDATE_TAGARR_LIST=true
#AUTOUPDATE_TAGARR_LIST_DIR=""

# tagarr_recover.sh — recover releaseGroup metadata from grab history
#AUTOUPDATE_TAGARR_RECOVER=true
#AUTOUPDATE_TAGARR_RECOVER_DIR=""

# tagarr_remove.sh — remove tagarr-added tags
#AUTOUPDATE_TAGARR_REMOVE=true
#AUTOUPDATE_TAGARR_REMOVE_DIR=""

# tagarr_rename.sh — rename release groups across the library
#AUTOUPDATE_TAGARR_RENAME=true
#AUTOUPDATE_TAGARR_RENAME_DIR=""
